      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{6}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{1458}, & 0\\le x\\le 9 \\\\ 1, & x>9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(1<X\\le 3).$",
      "worked_solution": "We can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X\\le 3) & =P(X\\le 3)-P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =F(3)-F(1) \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{6}-\\frac{{3}^{3}}{1458})-(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{1458}) \\\\  & =\\frac{230}{729}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
